    <string name="json_prompt_page_title">AI Prompt for JSON Conversion</string>
    <string name="json_prompt_page_desc">Copy this prompt to AI, then paste the returned JSON into the import box.</string>
    <string name="json_prompt_page_label">Conversion Prompt</string>
    <string name="json_prompt_back_button">Back to Import</string>
    <string name="json_prompt_usage_steps">1. Copy prompt  2. Paste into AI with your schedule  3. Paste returned JSON back to import page</string>
    <string name="json_prompt_content">You are a timetable JSON converter.\nConvert the user\'s timetable text into valid JSON for a mobile app.\nOnly output JSON. Do not output markdown or explanations.\n\nUse exactly this schema:\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"timezone\": \"Asia/Shanghai\",\n  \"courses\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Course Name\",\n      \"teacher\": \"Optional\",\n      \"dayOfWeek\": 1,\n      \"startTime\": \"08:00\",\n      \"endTime\": \"09:40\",\n      \"startWeek\": 1,\n      \"endWeek\": 16,\n      \"weekParity\": \"ALL\",\n      \"location\": \"Optional\",\n      \"note\": \"Optional\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n1. dayOfWeek must be 1-7 (1=Monday, 7=Sunday).\n2. startTime/endTime must be 24h HH:mm.\n3. startWeek/endWeek must be integers in range 1-30, and endWeek &gt;= startWeek.\n4. weekParity must be one of ALL, ODD, EVEN.\n5. Required fields: title, dayOfWeek, startTime, endTime. Optional fields may be empty strings.\n6. Keep all course entries, do not merge different time slots.</string>

